# Svelte & JS Conventions

- Svelte 5: use runes (`$props`, `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`) — not legacy `export let` / stores for new local state
- Keep pages thin: UI and page-local state in `src/pages/`; reusable logic in `src/lib/`
- One screen per file under `src/pages/<feature>/PascalCase.svelte`
- Public site screens: `src/pages/site/`; admin screens: `src/pages/admin/`
- Shared components: `src/lib/components/PascalCase.svelte`
- Plain JS modules (ESM). Prefer named exports
- Env: only `import.meta.env.VITE_*` (see `.env.example`)
- Desktop-first layouts for the corporate site and admin console

```svelte
<script>
  let { title = '' } = $props();
  let open = $state(false);
</script>
```

```js
// ✅ Domain helper
